# device_gap_version_fingerprint: Every version docs/testing.md 6.3 lists as valid (2-6, 10, 11, 20-22, 30, 31, 40-43, 60-62, 100-113, 200-209, 230-235, 237, 238, 245), then 0, 1 and 236, written in turn on a device with two display ports, each with EFI enabled just before it: 0x1200 shows whether the version kept EFI (efiDisplay from 3), 0x1034 what was negotiated, 0x122c the port count as the guest sees it (2 at 245, else count != 0) and 0x1234 the connection types (masked below 245). Then the same, downwards. 234 is not a case of features::features_for_version: it steps down to 233, so 48 versions are valid, not 49.
